@piece( JahDiffuseAlbedo )
// THE DIFFUSE LOBE'S DIRECTIONAL ALBEDO — what a surface under HlmsPbs's
// normalised Disney diffuse (Frostbite's energy-conserving form: the energy
// factor lerp( 1, 1 / 1.51, r ) and the retro-reflective fd90 = 0.5 r +
// 2 r (V.H)^2 scatter terms) actually reflects of a unit irradiance, as a
// fraction of what a Lambertian surface of the same albedo reflects
// (PHOTON-WRITER-1, P4 items ROUGHNESS-INTO-THE-VOXEL-STORE and THE EXACT
// ENVIRONMENT FACTOR). Stated once, read by three consumers:
//
//   * the pixel's ENVIRONMENT lobe (BRDF_EnvMap, 200.BRDFs_piece_ps.any): every
//     diffuse irradiance that reaches envColourD (the sky's SH, the voxel cones,
//     the irradiance field, the screen-probe gather) is reflected with
//     jahDiffuseAlbedo( NdotV, r ) — the lobe integrated over the incoming
//     hemisphere for a UNIFORM environment, by reciprocity the same function of
//     the view angle (0.686 at r = 1 at normal view, 1.031 at a grazing one);
//   * the LIGHT INJECTION (LightInjection_piece_cs.any): a voxel's surface lit by
//     a lamp at cos theta_l re-emits jahDiffuseAlbedo( cos theta_l, r ) of the
//     Lambertian answer, integrated over every outgoing direction — the voxel
//     holds what its surface renders, not rho E / pi;
//   * the BOUNCE (LightVctBounceInject_piece_cs.any) and the cards' relight: a
//     surface lit by the diffuse gather of its surroundings re-emits the
//     HEMISPHERICAL mean, jahDiffuseAlbedoHemi( r ) = 2 x the integral of
//     jahDiffuseAlbedo( mu, r ) mu dmu.
//
// THE INTEGRAL IN CLOSED FORM (REDS-1, 2026-10-29), not a fit. Because
// (V.H)^2 = ( 1 + V.L ) / 2, fd90 - 1 = k = ( 1.5 r - 1 ) + r V.L is LINEAR in
// the light direction, and the lobe is ef ( 1 + k a ) ( 1 + k b ) with
// a = ( 1 - N.L )^5, b = ( 1 - N.V )^5. Its cosine-weighted mean over the light's
// hemisphere needs only five moments of c = N.L under the weight 2c:
// E[a] = 1/21, E[c a] = 1/84, E[c^2 a] = 1/252, E[(1 - c^2) a] = 11/252, E[c] = 2/3,
// and E[cos^2 phi] = 1/2 for the azimuth (the odd powers vanish). With
// al = 1.5 r - 1 and v = N.V:
//     DA( v, r ) = ef [ 1 + b ( al + 2 r v / 3 ) + al / 21 + r v / 84
//                       + b ( al^2 / 21 + al r v / 42 + r^2 ( 11 - 9 v^2 ) / 504 ) ]
//     DA_hemi( r ) = ef [ 1 + 2 al / 21 + r / 63 + al^2 / 441 + al r / 3528 + 123 r^2 / 127008 ]
// exact to the float's rounding (DA_hemi( 1 ) = 0.705410, DA_hemi( 0 ) = 0.907029 =
// 400 / 441). The cubic this replaces was fitted to Ogre's DFG table
// (brtfLutDfg.dds, z), which sits up to 0.5 % under the lobe's own integral
// (0.701832 at r = 1): every bounce re-emitted 0.5 % too little, a room's
// series limit 0.27 % short (gi.bounce_series, gi.card_closed_form).
// Jahshaka's suites state the same function by their own quadrature of the
// lobe (enginetest::disneyDiffuseAlbedo), never by copying this text.
//
// IT LIVES IN THE FORK'S OWN PBS MEDIA (Hlms/Pbs/Any, parsed by every HlmsPbs, and
// listed by name by the two VCT jobs), so an HlmsPbs registered without
// Jahshaka's library - the VR spike's - still compiles BRDF_EnvMap.

float jahDiffuseAlbedo( float v, float r )
{
	v = clamp( v, 0.0, 1.0 );
	r = clamp( r, 0.0, 1.0 );
	float t = 1.0 - v;
	float t2 = t * t;
	float b = t2 * t2 * t;
	float al = 1.5 * r - 1.0;
	float rv = r * v;
	float ef = mix( 1.0, 1.0 / 1.51, r );
	return ef * ( 1.0 + al * ( 1.0 / 21.0 ) + rv * ( 1.0 / 84.0 )
	              + b * ( al + rv * ( 2.0 / 3.0 ) + al * al * ( 1.0 / 21.0 ) + al * rv * ( 1.0 / 42.0 )
	                      + r * r * ( 11.0 - 9.0 * v * v ) * ( 1.0 / 504.0 ) ) );
}

float jahDiffuseAlbedoHemi( float r )
{
	r = clamp( r, 0.0, 1.0 );
	float al = 1.5 * r - 1.0;
	float ef = mix( 1.0, 1.0 / 1.51, r );
	return ef * ( 1.0 + al * ( 2.0 / 21.0 ) + r * ( 1.0 / 63.0 ) + al * al * ( 1.0 / 441.0 )
	              + al * r * ( 1.0 / 3528.0 ) + r * r * ( 123.0 / 127008.0 ) );
}
@end
